Package: ocean-mist
Version: @VERSION@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: NahuelGenchi <65604505+NahuelGenchi@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-webkit2-4.1
Recommends: gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-libav
Suggests: firefox | firefox-esr
Homepage: https://github.com/NahuelGenchi/ocean-mist
Description: music player with the look of Windows Media Player 9
 Ocean Mist plays your music files and internet radio, and shows your
 YouTube Music and Apple Music libraries, in a window drawn like the classic
 Windows Media Player 9: the sculpted frame, the visualizations, a ten-band
 equalizer, a media library and playlists. It is an unofficial fan project,
 not affiliated with Microsoft.
 .
 Apple Music songs play in a playback engine that the player downloads when
 you ask it to, after a license screen. On Ubuntu 24.04 and later that engine
 needs a permission for its security sandbox. This package installs it as an
 AppArmor profile that names only the engine's file in your own data folder,
 so the player has nothing to ask you for.
 .
 YouTube Music and Apple Music sign in through Firefox, which this package
 only suggests.
